# Performance budget

Sources: `docs/SEO-PLAYBOOK.md` section 2 (CWV targets, "ship plain HTML with light JS", "reserve fixed-height slots for ad units"). Gates: `npm run audit:budgets` and `npm run lhci` (`lighthouserc.cjs`). Procedure: `performance-cwv-audit` skill.

## Targets (mobile, Lighthouse lab; field targets are p75)
- Performance >= 95, LCP <= 2.5 s, CLS <= 0.1, TBT <= 200 ms (INP <= 200 ms in the field), FCP <= 1.8 s.
- First-party JS <= 25 KB gzip per page (<= 15 KB on `/embed/*`), any single JS file <= 20 KB gzip, all JS <= 200 KB gzip.
- HTML document <= 60 KB gzip (CSS is inlined); inline CSS <= 25 KB gzip; any image <= 150 KB.

## Architecture constraints
- Static Astro output; `build.inlineStylesheets: 'always'`; one stylesheet (`src/styles/global.css`). Do not add Tailwind, Bootstrap, CSS-in-JS or a second stylesheet file.
- No UI framework (React/Vue/Svelte/Alpine/jQuery) and no charting/date/lodash libraries. Calculators are vanilla TS in Astro `<script>` blocks that import `src/lib/formulas/*` and `calc-utils.ts`. Dynamic `import()` only for rare, heavy features.
- No web fonts unless self-hosted, subset, `font-display: swap`, and one preloaded face. Default is the system font stack.
- No third-party scripts except GA4, AdSense and a certified CMP, each only when configured in `src/config/site.ts`, loaded `async`, with the CSP/host allow-list documented in `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`. `audit:budgets` fails other hosts.
- Content must be in the initial HTML; JS only powers inputs/results.
- Avoid `is:inline` scripts over ~6 KB gzip; avoid layout-thrashing handlers; debounce `input` handlers if work > ~10 ms.

## CLS rules
- Images: explicit `width`/`height` (or `aspect-ratio`); the LCP image (if any) is not `loading="lazy"` and has `fetchpriority="high"`.
- Ad slots: only `AdSlot.astro`; keep `.ad-slot` `min-height` (90 px) or the taller reserved height for the format actually served; never inject ads above the calculator or into the results panel; never collapse a slot after a no-fill.
- The cookie/consent banner overlays (fixed), it must not push content.
- Calculator results render with default values at first paint, or their container reserves height; charts have fixed dimensions.

## Process
- Any change to templates, CSS, calculator scripts, images or third-party tags: `npm run build && npm run audit:budgets && npm run lhci` and note the median metrics in the PR.
- Do not raise a budget to pass a PR. If a budget must move, change `scripts/audit/budgets.mjs` and `lighthouserc.cjs` together with written evidence of user benefit.
- Add one URL to `lighthouserc.cjs` per new **template**, not per page.
- CDN: hashed `/_astro/*` assets immutable for a year; HTML `max-age=0, must-revalidate` (`public/_headers`).
